# `EB-766`. Copies of the game's own `godot.log`, one per session, taken at
# teardown and at every detected boot stall (`understudy/soak_session.py`,
# `Session.archive_log`). Godot keeps five logs and rotates on launch, so a
# batch of relaunches erases the boot that went wrong before anybody reads it
# -- which is why the six stalled boots of 2026-09-15 have no logs at all.
#
# Same rule and the same reason as blindplay/ and seat/ next door: this is the
# ENGINE's raw output on this machine, kept so a failure can be read back, not
# evidence about a design. The excerpt that carried a finding goes in the
# commit message or the record; the file stays here.
*
!.gitignore
